<BaseLayout title="GPry interactive explainer" description="Explore a precomputed Gaussian-process active-learning run and see how GPry chooses expensive posterior evaluations."><header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive lab · GPry</span><h1>How does a surrogate learn?</h1><p>Move through a deterministic toy run. The target is fixed; the model’s mean, uncertainty and proposed next evaluation evolve as information arrives.</p></div></header><section class="shell lab-wrap"><GPryExplorer/><div class="prose"><h2>How to read it</h2><p>The dashed curve is the expensive target. GPry only sees the marked evaluations. The coral curve and band show its current surrogate belief; the acquisition rule balances promising regions against uncertainty to choose the next point.</p><p>This page replays precomputed states, so it is fast and reproducible. It illustrates the method rather than reporting a benchmark.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
